	<item>
		<title>Body chains</title>
		<link>/body/</link>
		<pubDate>2026-08-30 12:00:00</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[admin]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">/?p=107</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<div class="sec__head">
    
    <a class="sec__link" href="https://rexjewelz.vercel.app/shop.html">All 20 pieces</a>
  </div>
  <p class="cat__lead">Waist, belly, chest, harness, back and thigh. The pieces that take a size rather than a length.</p>

  <div class="twocol" style="margin-bottom:clamp(2rem,5vw,3.5rem)">
    <div>
      <p>These are the 12 pieces that sit on the body rather than hanging off it, and they are the reason the brand exists. A necklace only has to be the right length. A waist chain has to be the right size, sit at the right height, and still be there four hours later.</p>
      <p>That is a harder object to make and it is where most body chain fails. Ours carry their weight at the back, adjust at every join, and the thigh chain hides a silicone grip band because eleven versions without one all slid.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>Worn under a shirt nobody knows it is there. Worn over a slip it changes the whole outfit. Either way it is a layer, not the outfit, which is the part the photographs never quite tell you.</p>
      <p>Every piece here comes in three or four real sizes, and the full body chain can be built to your measurements. Take two minutes with a tape measure first, on the <a class="link" href="https://rexjewelz.vercel.app/fit.html">fit page</a>, and you will get it right the first time.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
      
