	<item>
		<title>Under $50</title>
		<link>/under-50/</link>
		<pubDate>2026-08-30 12:00:00</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[admin]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">/?p=108</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<div class="sec__head">
    
    <a class="sec__link" href="https://rexjewelz.vercel.app/shop.html">All 20 pieces</a>
  </div>
  <p class="cat__lead">8 pieces from $12, plus the starter set at $46. Nothing on this page is a lesser version of anything.</p>

  <div class="twocol" style="margin-bottom:clamp(2rem,5vw,3.5rem)">
    <div>
      <p>Cheap in this catalogue means small and simple, not badly made. The $12 anklet uses the same plated brass and the same clasp as the $169 body chain. There is less of it, and no stone setting, which is the entire reason for the price.</p>
      <p>What you should not buy first is the most expensive thing. Buy a waist chain, wear it under everything for a fortnight, and see how often you reach for it.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>The charms are the other honest way in. At $13 for one you can afford to choose badly, clip it onto a chain you already own, and decide later whether the rest is for you.</p>
      <p>Everything here still ships in 3 to 5 days and still carries the one year repair. Free shipping starts at $95, so two of these get you there.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
      <section class="sec" style="padding-bottom:0">
    <div class="sec__head">
      <h2 class="sec__h metal">Or take the <em>starter set</em></h2>
      <a class="sec__link" href="https://rexjewelz.vercel.app/sets.html">All sets</a>
    </div>
      </section>

